Title: Changing the image source using jQuery.
Body: <p>My DOM looks like this:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;div id="d1"&gt;
   &lt;div class="c1"&gt;
            &lt;a href="#"&gt;&lt;img src="img1_on.gif"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
            &lt;a href="#"&gt;&lt;img src="img2_on.gif"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
   &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>When someone clicks on an image, I want the image src to change to <code>&lt;img src="imgx_off.gif"&gt;</code> where <code>x</code> represents the image number 1 or 2.</p>

<p>Is this possible or do I have to use CSS to change the images?</p>

answer:
# Original HTML structure remains the same
html_structure = """
<div id="d1">
   <div class="c1">
            <a href="#" onclick="changeImage('img1'); return false;">&lt;img src="img1_on.gif"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
            <a href="#" onclick="changeImage('img2'); return false;">&lt;img src="img2_on.gif"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
   </div>
</div>
"""

# JavaScript function to change image source
javascript_function = """
<script type="text/javascript">
function changeImage(imgId) {
    var img = document.getElementById(imgId);
    if (img.src.indexOf('on') > -1) {
        img.src = img.src.replace('on', 'off');
    } else {
        img.src = img.src.replace('off', 'on');
    }
}
</script>
"""

# Updated HTML structure with inline JavaScript
updated_html = html_structure + javascript_function

# Print the updated HTML structure
print(updated_html)

